<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n28297" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mĕdēla</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mĕdella</span></b> , Lachm. ad <i><span class="en">Lucr. p.
		204</span></i>; Schol. Bob. ad Cic. Red. ad Quir.  p. 251, 8
		Bait.), ae, f.
		medeor, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a healing, cure, a remedy</i> (post-class.).
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">facere medelam,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Gell.
					12, 5, 3</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">facere medelarum miracula,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					16, 11, 2</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vulneribus medelas adhibere,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">App. M. 8, p. 210, 4</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>, <i>a remedy, means of
				redress</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">legum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Gell. 20, 1, 22</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Aus. Prof. 15</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">quibus rebus veluti medela adventus Alexandri
					fuit,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Just.
					11, 1, 7</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
